@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] terminal-bytes-never-at-rest
Terminal input/output bytes MUST NOT enter the database, logs, audit versions
or job arguments. The registry stores identity fields only; the audit events
store actor, session and kind receipts only.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] terminal-authority-per-operation
Terminal capability MUST be rechecked for every open and ticket: a fresh host
report advertising terminal protocol 2, current Cedar read (write for rw),
and a registry session bound to the current placement and execution epoch.
Tickets are single-use, short-lived and mode-bound.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol] stream-controls-require-placement
Every VM-scoped control sent to a host stream MUST carry the exact placement
and execution epoch; input frames MUST carry strictly increasing per-channel
sequences so replays cannot execute twice.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity;recovery] terminal-peer-budget-incarnation-is-explicit
Incoming and outgoing peer processes MUST acquire from the configured local
peer-budget server, retain the returned budget incarnation, monitor that exact
process, and release the same incarnation on termination. The default server
MUST remain `Marshall.Terminal.PeerBudget`; an isolated validated server MAY be
selected for a test fixture without changing production capacity settings. An
adapter boundary that can consume the callback's monitor message MUST also
terminate its transport owner when that incarnation disappears.
